  "chain": "corrosion between field-lead lugs [cause B] -> bolted connection failure at brush rigging/panel wiring -> partial loss of EDG-1 load during surveillance test AND increased electrical stress on field insulation -> first coil on nearest pole grounds -> EDG-1 declared inoperable, AOT exceeded -> TS 3.16.B.1.a.3/3.0.2 violation (operation prohibited by Technical Specifications) for ~8 days",
  "golden_questions": [
    "Q1",
    "Q3",
    "Q4",
    "Q14"
  ],
  "notes": "No EIIS code given for field lead, rotor, or exciter beyond [EXC]; EK used for the emergency switchgear/EDG system per block-13 system code. Common-cause verification runs of EDG-2 and EDG-3 modeled as corrective actions, not BACKED_UP_BY, since EDG-1 supported specific shared loads (AFW cross-tie, filter fans, MCR chiller) rather than being interchangeable with EDG-2/3 for its own bus; no explicit statement that EDG-2/3 remained available to cover EDG-1's specific loads during the outage, so BACKED_UP_BY edges were omitted per rule 6. TS 3.6.1.3 entry noted as regulatory reference tied to AFW cross-tie loss of power source."
